    {
      "source_handle": "P0478",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0478",
        "source_id": "source::P0478",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Cross-cohort gut microbiome associations with immune checkpoint inhibitor response in advanced melanoma",
        "doi": "10.1038/s41591-022-01695-5",
        "paper_id": "d4c18d58cffce0cab6831c84535e02c608d4db49",
        "year": "2022",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "This study investigates the association between baseline gut microbiome features and clinical response to ICIs in advanced melanoma. By integrating shotgun metagenomic sequencing data from five newly recruited cohorts (n=165) with 147 samples from previously published studies, the authors aimed to reconcile conflicting findings from smaller single-cohort studies. The research employed multivariate statistical analyses, machine learning models (Lasso), and meta-analysis approaches to identify microbial taxa and functions associated with overall response rate (ORR) and progression-free survival at 12 months (PFS12). The work highlights that while the microbiome is relevant to ICI response, these associations are highly cohort-dependent, with limited reproducibility of specific biomarkers or predictive signatures across different populations."
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch7"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U1_跨癌种关联图谱"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0170",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0170",
        "source_id": "source::P0170",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Enterotype-specific microbial biomarkers of immune checkpoint inhibitor response revealed by large-scale integrated metagenomic analysis",
        "doi": "10.1007/s00262-026-04432-w",
        "paper_id": "4a1e10851c0bf838d11646a65bc0ee57b10b940a",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "该研究提出肠道菌群并非均匀分布，而是组织为不同的“肠型”（enterotypes），假设这种分层可以揭示对免疫治疗反应的特定微生物标志物。作者首先通过PAM算法将569个样本聚类为两个主要肠型（E1和E2）及其亚群。随后，利用LEfSe分析识别各肠型中响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的特异性物种标志物，共发现166种特异性物种。为了初步验证这些标志物的稳健性，作者在意大利Modena癌症中心的一个包含19名具有卓越且持久反应患者的独立队列（MOC）中进行了探索性一致性评估。此外，研究还应用多种机器学习算法构建分类模型，以评估基于微生物组特征预测治疗反应的潜力。结果显示，虽然整体预测性能中等，但在特定亚组和独立队列中表现出一定的一致性，支持了基于肠型进行患者分层的探索性框架。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U1_跨癌种关联图谱"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0289",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0289",
        "source_id": "source::P0289",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Microbiome Landscape and Association with Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Advanced Solid Tumors: A SCRUM-Japan MONSTAR-SCREEN Study",
        "doi": "10.1158/2767-9764.crc-24-0543",
        "paper_id": "7fe882e8b39d1a041fd2fee47d9321c965f01aa5",
        "year": "2025",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本研究利用大规模全国性筛查项目的数据，旨在阐明晚期实体瘤患者肠道微生物组的景观及其对ICI疗效的影响。研究首先分析了化疗前患者的微生物组特征，发现上消化道肿瘤（尤其是术后胃癌和胰腺癌）及PPI使用者粪便中口腔细菌比例显著升高。随后，在ICI治疗队列中，研究发现整体α多样性（ASV计数、Shannon指数）与ICI疗效无显著关联，这与部分既往单一癌种研究的结论不同。然而，粪便中高比例的口腔细菌与较短的无进展生存期（PFS）显著相关。进一步分析显示，这种负面影响在同时使用PPI的患者中更为明显，提示PPI诱导的口腔细菌易位可能是降低ICI疗效的重要机制之一。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch4"
      ],
