    {
      "source_handle": "P0148",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0148",
        "source_id": "source::P0148",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Response to immune checkpoint inhibition is associated with the gut microbiome in advanced KRAS-mutated non-small cell lung cancer",
        "doi": "10.1101/2023.10.30.23297712",
        "paper_id": "42b8755a18f7ff2ebb90765b502a37b6f6e868e5",
        "year": "2023",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "This study investigates the association between the gut microbiome and clinical outcomes in a homogeneous cohort of advanced KRAS-mutated NSCLC patients receiving ICI therapy. The authors performed shotgun metagenomic sequencing on baseline stool samples to analyze microbial composition and functional pathways. They compared responders versus non-responders (defined by DCR and PFS12) and patients with vs. without immune-related adverse events (irAEs), adjusting for confounders like ICI regimen, metastatic stage, age, sex, and BMI. The study found no differences in overall alpha or beta diversity but identified specific species and metabolic pathways differentially abundant between groups."
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch4",
        "Ch5"
      ],
      "unit_links": [],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0474",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0474",
        "source_id": "source::P0474",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Tumor microenvironment-mediated resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors in non-small cell lung cancer: Mechanisms, combination strategies and clinical perspectives (Review)",
        "doi": "10.3892/mco.2026.2971",
        "paper_id": "d227bde3dc62e02cfe87a58fa5173e149048ed4e",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本文是一篇叙事性综述，旨在将TME介导的ICI耐药视为一个相互连接的生物学过程，而非孤立因素的集合。文章系统梳理了免疫抑制细胞群、基质重塑、血管功能障碍、缺氧、代谢重编程以及抗原呈递缺陷和致癌驱动信号如何协同作用，形成免疫沙漠、免疫排斥或耗竭性炎症表型。在此基础上，综述评估了针对这些机制的联合治疗策略，区分了III期支持的临床标准与早期探索性方法，并提出了整合PD-L1、TMB、干扰素γ特征、空间组学、ctDNA等指标的操作化生物标志物框架，以指导NSCLC的精准免疫治疗。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch4",
        "Ch5"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "unit_id": "Ch5_U02"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0271",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0271",
        "source_id": "source::P0271",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "The role of the gut microbiome on the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in Japanese responder patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer.",
        "doi": "10.21037/tlcr.2019.10.23",
        "paper_id": "753e796b9f6fe2fe78f1b4c6074d39441710eda7",
        "year": "2019",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本研究旨在探讨肠道微生物组组成与晚期NSCLC患者对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效之间的关联。研究回顾性分析了17名在日本京都府立医科大学接受ICI治疗且持续时间超过3个月的患者的粪便样本。通过16S rRNA基因测序分析肠道菌群多样性及物种丰度，并结合临床疗效数据（基于RECIST 1.1标准定义的响应状态及治疗失败时间TTF），比较了反应者与非反应者在肠道微生物组成上的差异，并评估特定细菌属的丰度与临床预后指标的相关性。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch4",
        "Ch5"
      ],
      "unit_links": [],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0578",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0578",
        "source_id": "source::P0578",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial",
        "doi": "10.1136/jitc-2026-015122",
        "paper_id": "d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本研究是一项单臂IIa期篮子试验（MITRIC），旨在验证通过FMT调节肠道微生物群能否克服已建立的ICI耐药性。研究纳入了12名在转移性阶段对ICI治疗进展的患者，使用ICI长期响应者作为供体，给予患者最多五次FMT（前两次通过结肠镜，后续通过灌肠），并继续原有ICI治疗。主要终点为FMT相关不良事件和客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示FMT安全性良好，但未能观察到客观肿瘤反应（ORR为0%），仅5名患者达到疾病稳定。尽管缺乏总体疗效证据，研究发现FMT诱导了短暂的微生物定植，且外周血中的免疫细胞特征（如分化T细胞与髓系细胞的平衡）与生存期显著相关，但这些免疫特征似乎更多反映疾病本身状态而非FMT的特异性干预效果。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch5",
        "Ch6"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        },
        {
