        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Adverse Effect of the Duration of Antibiotic Use Prior to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors on the Overall Survival of Patients with Recurrent Gynecologic Malignancies",
        "doi": "10.3390/cancers15245745",
        "paper_id": "9cfb62b17064ed5abe1c447f8fa2f46e716b6c0d",
        "year": "2023",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "This retrospective cohort study evaluated the association between prior antibiotic use and oncological outcomes in patients with recurrent gynecologic cancers receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). The study analyzed clinical data from 215 patients to determine if antibiotic exposure within 60 days before ICI initiation affected disease control rate (DCR) and overall survival (OS). It identified a cumulative antibiotic duration of >14 days as an independent predictor of poor OS, while noting that DCR was not significantly altered by antibiotic use. The authors attribute these findings to potential gut microbiota dysbiosis induced by prolonged antibiotic therapy."
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U2_外部干扰与宿主背景"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0157",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0157",
        "source_id": "source::P0157",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Overcoming Resistance Mechanisms to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors: Leveraging the Anti-Tumor Immune Response",
        "doi": "10.3390/curroncol31010001",
        "paper_id": "45ca27020bec6c917c6b71d8b1bad217f5abd0ed",
        "year": "2023",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本文是一篇综述文章，旨在系统梳理T细胞介导的抗肿瘤免疫反应原理，分析癌症细胞对ICIs产生原发性或获得性耐药的多种机制，并探讨逆转这些耐药性的治疗策略。文章首先回顾了从Coley毒素到现代ICI的发展历程，随后详细阐述了T细胞激活、浸润肿瘤微环境（TME）、效应功能及维持免疫记忆的过程。在此基础上，文章将耐药机制按免疫激活的连续阶段进行分类：包括免疫细胞进入TME受阻、抗肿瘤免疫反应启动失败、效应功能减弱以及免疫反应无法持续。此外，还讨论了宿主因素如肠道微生物群和合并用药对ICI疗效的影响。最后，文章总结了多种克服耐药的策略，包括增强肿瘤免疫原性、改善免疫抑制性微环境、逆转T细胞耗竭、联合小分子抑制剂以及调节肠道微生物群等。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U2_外部干扰与宿主背景"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0033",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0033",
        "source_id": "source::P0033",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Longitudinal gut microbiome changes in immune checkpoint blockade-treated advanced melanoma",
        "doi": "10.1038/s41591-024-02803-3",
        "paper_id": "0f25b980517704cd7fa782dd9e51d16b77d00249",
        "year": "2024",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "该研究旨在解决既往横断面研究中微生物标志物缺乏共识的问题，通过纵向追踪ICB治疗期间肠道微生物组的动态变化，区分长期无进展生存（PFS ≥12个月）与短期生存患者的微生物特征。研究利用贝叶斯回归模型分析物种水平基因组箱（SGBs）和代谢通路的丰度轨迹，并考察不同临床情境（如治疗方案、结肠炎发生、质子泵抑制剂使用）对微生物动态的影响。研究发现，除了基线差异外，许多微生物在治疗后的丰度变化模式具有预测价值，且同一微生物在不同临床背景下可能呈现相反的动态趋势。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
