    {
      "source_handle": "P0200",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0200",
        "source_id": "source::P0200",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Integrative stratification of response to immunotherapy using host and microbial signatures in patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer",
        "doi": "10.1186/s13073-026-01736-5",
        "paper_id": "57133de914bfeefa962dacc91943374147c07fff",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "该研究针对肠道微生物组与ICI疗效关联中纵向多组学数据不足的现状，对92例晚期NSCLC患者进行了纵向采样和多组学分析。通过比较患者与健康人的微生物特征，并利用内部队列及728例公共数据开发并验证了一个分类评分系统。研究发现特定菌群丰度与治疗反应相关，观察到治疗过程中微生物失调的动态变化，并提出了一个结合肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）的跨人群评分以改善疗效分层。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U3_动态监测与纵向演变"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0205",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0205",
        "source_id": "source::P0205",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Correlation of distribution characteristics and dynamic changes of gut microbiota with the efficacy of immunotherapy in EGFR-mutated non-small cell lung cancer",
        "doi": "10.1186/s12967-024-05135-5",
        "paper_id": "590fbadadd7e854b3435c77a34e74cd5b744c084",
        "year": "2024",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "This prospective cohort study investigated the impact of gut microbiota and metabolites on the efficacy of ICIs in a specific subgroup of NSCLC patients with EGFR mutations. The research enrolled 74 advanced EGFR+ NSCLC patients and collected detailed clinical data regarding antibiotic and probiotic usage. Fecal samples were dynamically collected from 18 patients at four time points: baseline, early on-treatment, response, and progression. Metagenomic next-generation sequencing and ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (UHPLC-MS) were employed to analyze microbial composition and metabolic profiles. The study aimed to identify biomarkers and mechanisms linking the gut environment to ICI outcomes in this population, which is often considered immunologically 'cold'."
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U3_动态监测与纵向演变"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0415",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0415",
        "source_id": "source::P0415",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Relating the gut metagenome and metatranscriptome to immunotherapy responses in melanoma patients",
        "doi": "10.1186/s13073-019-0672-4",
        "paper_id": "b63bda99b7dbfd8c9d82d9a7246125da767de5c7",
        "year": "2019",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本研究旨在探究肠道微生物群对黑色素瘤免疫治疗疗效的影响。通过对27名患者的治疗前粪便样本进行多组学分析，研究发现较高的微生物群落丰富度与较长的无进展生存期相关。基于整体微生物组成的聚类分析将患者分为高、中、低风险组，其中低风险组的疾病进展风险显著低于高风险组。在物种层面，拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）中的部分菌种（如B. ovatus, B. dorei）与较短的PFS相关，而粪杆菌属（Faecalibacterium）中的F. prausnitzii等则与较长的PFS相关。此外，研究首次结合宏转录组数据，识别出与PFS相关的宏基因组功能通路及其转录表达，包括L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸生物合成和B族维生素生物合成等风险相关通路，以及异亮氨酸生物合成等保护相关通路。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U3_动态监测与纵向演变"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0485",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0485",
        "source_id": "source::P0485",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Abstract B023: Delineating the role of the microbiome and tumor microenvironment interactions driving mucosal melanoma (MM) response and resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) treatment",
        "doi": "10.1158/1538-7445.rareca26-b023",
        "paper_id": "da741d94b4d509b96c9490a118677edf3d1417a7",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "该研究旨在阐明微生物组与肿瘤微环境相互作用如何驱动黏膜黑色素瘤对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的响应与耐药。研究在MD安德森癌症中心前瞻性纳入MM患者，收集粪便、黏膜拭子及肿瘤组织样本进行多组学分析。初步结果显示，不同原发部位的MM具有特定的微生物特征和突变谱；在接受ICI治疗的患者中，响应者与非响应者在肠道菌群组成上存在差异，且响应者肿瘤微环境中CD56和CD20表达更高。这是一项正在进行中的研究，目前提供了部分基线数据和初步关联结果。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U3_动态监测与纵向演变"
        }
      ],
