    {
      "source_handle": "P0327",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0327",
        "source_id": "source::P0327",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Biomarkers of Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Non-Small-Cell Lung Cancer: Microbiota Composition, Short-Chain Fatty Acids, and Intestinal Permeability",
        "doi": "10.3390/cancers16061144",
        "paper_id": "8b3aa2316f5ec9089bf4d5f6cefbb1c1be74ad79",
        "year": "2024",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "empirical"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本研究旨在识别NSCLC患者中预测ICI疗效和毒性的生物标志物，重点考察肠道微环境。研究招募了55名接受不同ICI方案（如Durvalumab, Pembrolizumab等）的III期或IV期NSCLC患者，在基线时收集粪便和血液样本。通过16S rDNA扩增测序分析肠道菌群组成，利用GC-MS测定粪便中的短链脂肪酸含量，并通过血浆检测瓜氨酸、抗瓜氨酸抗体、Zonulin和内毒素水平来评估肠道屏障通透性。统计分析包括描述性统计、生存分析（Kaplan-Meier）、相关性分析及LEfSe差异分析。结果显示，尽管患者肠道菌群丰富多样且功能均一，但未能发现任何肠道微生物组成、代谢产物或通透性指标与ICI治疗反应或irAE发生之间的显著相关性。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U3_动态监测与纵向演变"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0546",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0546",
        "source_id": "source::P0546",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Gut microbiome in modulating immune checkpoint inhibitors",
        "doi": "10.1016/j.ebiom.2022.104163",
        "paper_id": "f32b23ec68d527d1114ddf96e609079a09947e6e",
        "year": "2022",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本文是一篇综述，旨在总结肠道微生物组在调节宿主免疫和癌症治疗反应中的最新知识。文章首先阐述了肠道微生物如何通过局部和全身途径影响宿主免疫系统（包括先天性和适应性免疫），并进一步讨论其在肿瘤微环境（TME）中对抗肿瘤免疫的作用。随后，文章评估了通过粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌、益生元以及饮食和生活方式改变来调节肠道微生物群以改善ICIs疗效的临床前证据和临床试验进展，并讨论了相关的安全性和未来挑战。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch5"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U3_动态监测与纵向演变"
        },
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "unit_id": "Ch5_U05"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0026",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0026",
        "source_id": "source::P0026",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Clinical potential of the gut microbiome in oncology: a scoping review of treatment response, toxicity and biomarker development",
        "doi": "10.1007/s00520-026-10918-1",
        "paper_id": "0cf91befe63ec25329391e50e90d14093d3c74d7",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "这是一篇遵循JBI指南和PRISMA-ScR报告的范围综述（scoping review），旨在系统映射并批判性地描述当前关于肠道微生物组在肿瘤学中作为生物标志物的证据。作者检索了2015年至2025年间发表的20项相关研究，涵盖了观察性队列、临床试验和机制研究。综述重点分析了特定微生物类群如何影响免疫治疗和化疗的疗效，以及它们对治疗相关毒性的调节作用。研究发现，基于微生物组的预测模型在某些情况下优于传统临床标记物（如尿路上皮癌中AUC达0.88 vs 0.50），且特定干预（如益生菌）可减轻毒性。然而，综述也指出，由于方法学异质性、缺乏外部验证和机制理解不完整，这些模型的临床转化仍面临挑战。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch7"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        },
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "unit_id": "Ch7_U03"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0144",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0144",
        "source_id": "source::P0144",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Gut Microbiome Control of Tumor Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Response: Mechanistic Insights and Clinical Translation",
        "doi": "10.54254/2753-8818/2026.es36576",
        "paper_id": "412cf94675e5be84f181d1075570015bc0b66c25",
        "year": "2026",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本文是一篇综述，旨在总结肠道微生物群影响ICIs疗效和毒性的现有机制证据，并探讨靶向微生物群的潜在治疗策略。文章首先阐述了肠道作为免疫界面的解剖学和生理学基础，随后详细讨论了特定有益菌属（如Akkermansia muciniphila、Bacteroides）及其代谢产物（短链脂肪酸SCFAs、肌苷、色氨酸代谢物）如何通过调节先天性和适应性免疫反应来增强抗肿瘤免疫。此外，文章分析了微生物群通过肠-肺轴等途径参与irAEs（特别是结肠炎和肺炎）的机制，并重点评估了粪便微生物移植（FMT）在治疗难治性ICI相关结肠炎中的临床应用现状、疗效、安全性及局限性。最后，文章指出了当前研究在标准化和可重复性方面的不足，并提出了未来结合多组学和人工智能进行精准医疗的方向。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0161",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0161",
        "source_id": "source::P0161",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Modulation of gut microbiota: a novel approach to enhancing the effects of immune checkpoint inhibitors",
        "doi": "10.1177/17588359231204854",
        "paper_id": "478e06158ac52abb764c678cb77109164cd00f5d",
        "year": "2023",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本文是一篇综述，旨在系统梳理肠道微生物群与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效之间的关联。文章首先阐述了肠道微生物群作为影响ICI耐药性的关键因素，总结了反应者与非反应者之间微生物组成的差异，并定义了“有利”和“不利”的微生物特征。随后，文章详细评估了通过粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌/菌群联合体以及饮食干预等手段调节肠道微生物群以增强ICI疗效的临床前和临床研究进展。此外，论文还探讨了这种调节作用对免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响，并归纳了包括分子模拟、模式识别受体激活、代谢物释放及肿瘤内微生物组调控在内的多种潜在作用机制。最后，文章指出了当前研究在供体选择、标准化、机制验证等方面的局限性，并提出了未来研究方向。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0291",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0291",
        "source_id": "source::P0291",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "Role of the intestinal microbiome and microbial-derived metabolites in immune checkpoint blockade immunotherapy of cancer",
        "doi": "10.1186/s13073-021-00923-w",
        "paper_id": "8084192e33a8c5d78c74149b0e22d13f2ca24771",
        "year": "2021",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "This paper reviews the emerging evidence linking the gut microbiome to the efficacy and toxicity of immune checkpoint blockade immunotherapy. It synthesizes findings from preclinical models and clinical studies to identify specific bacterial taxa and metabolites associated with ICI response or resistance. The authors discuss two main mechanistic categories: antigen-independent modulation of innate and adaptive immunity, and antigen-specific cross-reactivity between microbial and tumor antigens. Additionally, the review examines the negative impact of antibiotic use on ICI efficacy and the potential of fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) to restore responsiveness or treat colitis. It highlights inconsistencies across studies regarding specific beneficial bacteria and calls for larger prospective interventional trials to establish microbiome-based biomarkers and therapeutic strategies."
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0387",
      "identity": {
