          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "本文是一篇综述，旨在评估通过调节肠道微生物群来增强固体肿瘤免疫治疗疗效的潜力。文章系统回顾了基于单菌株/有限混合物的益生菌（如CBM588、EDP1503）、多菌株微生物菌群组合（如MET4、SER-401、VE800）以及全环境粪便微生物移植（FMT）在联合ICI治疗中的临床试验结果。研究重点分析了不同干预策略在客观缓解率（ORR）、无进展生存期（mPFS）及安全性方面的表现，并探讨了从动物模型到人体转化的挑战、监管障碍、患者招募困难以及现有机制理解的局限性。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch5"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        },
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "unit_id": "Ch5_U03"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0470",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0470",
        "source_id": "source::P0470",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "The impact of gut microbiota modulation on responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer.",
        "doi": "10.1556/030.2025.02719",
        "paper_id": "d01d7681c26311e53a792fec4a5c6d8c608be0d6",
        "year": "2025",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "该论文是一篇系统综述和荟萃分析，旨在评估肠道微生物群对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。作者通过系统检索PubMed、Embase、Web of Science和Cochrane Library数据库（截至2025年3月），纳入了38项涉及5,642名患者的研究。研究重点分析了特定细菌属（如Akkermansia muciniphila、Bifidobacterium longum、Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）的富集、抗生素使用、供体反应者粪便微生物移植（FMT）以及微生物多样性指数与总生存期（OS）、无进展生存期（PFS）、客观缓解率（ORR）及irAEs之间的关联。结果显示，有益菌富集与改善生存预后显著相关，而抗生素暴露则与较差的生存结果相关，FMT从反应者来源可显著提高缓解率。"
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1"
      ],
      "unit_links": [
        {
          "chapter_id": "Ch1",
          "unit_id": "U4_证据阶梯与转化边界"
        }
      ],
      "review_source_handles": []
    },
    {
      "source_handle": "P0573",
      "identity": {
        "source_handle": "P0573",
        "source_id": "source::P0573",
        "aliases": [],
        "title": "From chaos to order: optimizing fecal microbiota transplantation for enhanced immune checkpoint inhibitors efficacy",
        "doi": "10.1080/19490976.2025.2452277",
        "paper_id": "ff51b7d7a956ceb17d4fb9e0f36c3446c6a4cf65",
        "year": "2025",
        "canonical_paper_id": null
      },
      "source_types": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.paper_kind",
          "value": "review"
        }
      ],
      "content_clues": [
        {
          "field": "study_summary_A.work_summary",
          "value": "This is a comprehensive narrative review that critically examines the controversial effects of combining FMT with ICIs. It synthesizes evidence from clinical trials and preclinical studies to explain why FMT sometimes enhances ICI efficacy while other times shows no benefit or adverse effects. The paper outlines mechanisms involving gut microbiota modulation, metabolite profiles, and tumor microenvironment changes, and discusses factors influencing outcomes such as donor selection, recipient characteristics, and administration protocols. It concludes by proposing future research directions including large-scale trials, multi-omics integration, and alternative microbiome-based therapies."
        }
      ],
      "chapter_ids": [
        "Ch1",
        "Ch2",
        "Ch5"
      ],
